      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t directly set the state, right? It instead queues a transition to the given state?\n\nI think it\u0027s important to be precise about what this does because the rules around when it\u0027s valid to make a transition are somewhat complex, and being more descriptive around the later \"only one state transition\" line would probably be useful.\n\nMore generally, I\u0027d appreciate a comment block (probably up at the top) explaining how the state transitions are meant to go, since it seems like `sm_run_state` is expected to occur shortly after `set_state` but it\u0027s hard to tell just from the API documentation.",
